.TH LORA_MERGE 1 "2026-06-29" "Symoneural" "Symoneural Helper Utilities"
.SH NAME
lora_merge \- merge LoRA adapter weights into a base model checkpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python helpers/python/lora_merge.py
.I base
.I lora
.I output
.RB [ \-\-alpha
.IR FLOAT ]
.RB [ \-\-style
.BR peft | kohya ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lora_merge.py
merges a LoRA adapter
.I .safetensors
file into a base model
.I .safetensors
file and writes the merged checkpoint to
.IR output .
The merge formula is:
.IP
W_merged = W_base + alpha * (B @ A)
.PP
Two LoRA adapter styles are supported:
.TP
.B peft
PEFT-style adapters storing
.B lora_A.weight
and
.B lora_B.weight
tensors under
.BR base_model.model.<layer> .
.TP
.B kohya
Kohya-style adapters storing
.B lora_down.weight
and
.B lora_up.weight
tensors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I base
Base model
.I .safetensors
file path.
.TP
.I lora
LoRA adapter
.I .safetensors
file path.
.TP
.I output
Destination path for the merged
.I .safetensors
file.
.TP
.B \-\-alpha \fIFLOAT\fR
LoRA merge scale factor (default:
.BR 1.0 ).
Typical value is
.B lora_alpha / lora_rank
from the adapter config.
.TP
.B \-\-style \fB{peft,kohya}\fR
Adapter format style (default:
.BR peft ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Merge a PEFT adapter:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/lora_merge.py base.safetensors adapter.safetensors merged.safetensors
.EE
.RE
.PP
Merge a Kohya-style LoRA with custom alpha:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/lora_merge.py base.safetensors kohya.safetensors merged.safetensors \e
    \-\-style kohya \-\-alpha 0.75
.EE
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Shape mismatches and missing base keys are printed to
.B stderr
and skipped without aborting the merge.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B safetensors
(pip install safetensors),
.B numpy
(pip install numpy).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tensor_utils (1),
.BR gguf_inspect (1)
